---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import { LINKS } from './links';
import FlowDiagram from './FlowDiagram.astro';
import MaskDemo from './MaskDemo.astro';

const steps = [
	{ title: 'Intercept', text: 'Requests reach Shadow through <code>HTTPS_PROXY</code>, a gateway base URL or the Rust API. Only known AI hosts are decrypted; everything else is tunnelled untouched.' },
	{ title: 'Detect', text: 'Checksummed patterns, emails, phones, secrets, hostnames, IPs and paths, your own dictionary of customers and codenames, and optional local NER or Presidio.' },
	{ title: 'Translate', text: 'Each value gets a consistent, format-preserving fake from your machine’s persona, or a typed token for bulk reports. Secrets can be redacted outright.' },
	{ title: 'Restore', text: 'Fakes in the answer are turned back into real values: full responses, streamed tokens and tool-call arguments, before your tool sees them.' },
];
---

<Section
	id="how-it-works"
	eyebrow="How it works"
	title="Translate, don’t block"
	lead="Shadow sits between your tools and the model. The provider gets a coherent prompt about people who do not exist. You get the answer about the real ones, and when the goal is to write to someone, the model sees who."
>
	<FlowDiagram />
	<MaskDemo />
	<div class="hp-notes">
		<div>
			<h3>The clinical meaning survives.</h3>
			<p>The model never needs the real identity to summarise a note, so it only ever sees a stand-in patient.</p>
		</div>
		<div>
			<h3>Same shape, same fake.</h3>
			<p>NHS numbers still pass their checksum, phones stay phones, and a value always maps to the same fake.</p>
		</div>
		<div>
			<h3>Intent-aware.</h3>
			<p>
				Ask it to write to someone, such as “email Dr Okafor about Maria’s results”, and the recipient is passed through so
				the model writes to the right person; the patient is still masked. <a class="hp-inline" href={LINKS.intent}>How intent works</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<ol class="hp-steps hp-steps--spaced">
		{
			steps.map((s, i) => (
				<li>
					<span class="hp-steps__n">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
					<h3>{s.title}</h3>
					<p set:html={s.text} />
				</li>
			))
		}
	</ol>
	<a class="hp-more" href={LINKS.howItWorks}>Read the full request lifecycle <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
</Section>
